"""Replace explanatory narration with observable phone and farewell scenes."""

def apply_phone_and_letter_edits(edits):
    edits[9]['-d'].update({
        15: ('不是查，是看散场以后谁留下收。', "Not checking them—seeing who stays to put them away afterwards."),
    })
    edits[9].setdefault('-r', {}).update({
        4: ('晚间开放也把收尾的工作带到了大家眼前。平时六点停止借书，工作人员六点半收完；活动那晚读者八点离开，两名工作人员还要把椅子收回、检查热水设备、关好门窗，到八点半才结束。每人比平时多值班两个小时，四次合起来是十六个人小时，每人八小时。读者可以帮忙排椅子，设备和门窗仍由工作人员检查。最后一次收完，馆员把四晚的值班表摊在桌上，说下个月要是继续，还得先问这两个人有没有时间。发起活动的读者拿出手机，约好第二天再来一起看安排。', "Evening events made closing duties visible. Lending normally ended at six and staff finished at 6:30. On event nights readers left at eight; two staff put chairs away, checked the hot-water equipment and closed the windows and doors until 8:30. Each worked two extra hours per event: sixteen staff-hours over four evenings, or eight extra hours each. Readers helped with chairs, while staff checked equipment and doors. After the final evening, the librarian spread out the duty rota: continuing next month would first depend on those two people's availability. The organisers arranged to return the next day to look at the schedule together."),
    })
    edits[10].setdefault('-d', {}).update({
        4: ('我倒想先读。两位演奏的朋友也想先听一段。', "I'd prefer reading first. The two performers also want to hear a passage before playing."),
    })
    edits[10]['-r'].update({
        1: ('这次协会愿意借小厅给我们办读书和听歌活动，日期还得等会长周五确认。我先把今天的议题缩到节目顺序，场地和设备由两个人另外联系。讨论安排四十分钟，我把剩下时间写在纸角上，免得一开口就忘了。有人想先听歌，让陌生人容易坐下来；有人想先读，让两位演奏的朋友也能听一段，再上去唱。他们八点以后不能留，朗读就不能太长。我先问清是哪两个人，把八点写在节目单旁边。', "The association offered its small hall, with the date awaiting the president's Friday confirmation. Today's forty-minute meeting covered running order; two others would check the room and equipment. I noted the time left. Some wanted music first to help newcomers settle; others wanted reading first so the two performers could hear a passage before playing. They couldn't stay past eight, so the reading couldn't run too long. I checked who they were and wrote eight beside the programme."),
    })
    edits[10].setdefault('-paired-reading', {}).update({
        1: ('今天讨论节目先后，我先说想把读书放前面，好让两位演奏的朋友先听一段，再上去唱。他们八点以后要走，我提议朗读短一点，给歌留够时间。主持人问清是谁以后，把八点写在节目单旁边。有人建议开头一首、后面一首，我看着纸上的两个位置，觉得也可以试。我点了点头，让陈宇去问问那两个人。陈宇拿起手机，说先联系他们，周四晚饭以前给消息，我就把原来画的两段改成三个位置，等回复再排。', "I suggested reading first so the two performers could hear a passage before playing. They had to leave after eight, so I proposed a short reading with enough time left for music. The host checked who they were and noted eight on the programme. One song at the start and one later was another option. I nodded for Chen Yu to ask both performers. He'd contact them and message before Thursday's dinner. I changed my two blocks to three slots while waiting for their reply."),
    })
    edits[11]['-r'].update({
        0: ('演出散场，我站在门边给林安打电话。她那边有车经过，后面几个人一边走一边笑。我问她在哪，她说车还没到，先别等我，你们进去。我只抓住别等两个字，马上问不去了。她提高声音说不是不去，晚点到。我让她把后半句再说一遍，这回总算听清。陈宇已经走到店门口，回头问我还等不等，我说我们先进去，她等到车就发消息。我拿起包，赶紧跟上他。', "After the show I called Lin An from the doorway. Traffic passed at her end while people behind me laughed on their way out. Her bus hadn't arrived; we should go inside without waiting. Catching only 'don't wait,' I asked if she wasn't coming. She raised her voice: she was coming, just later. I asked her to repeat the second half and finally heard it. Chen Yu, already at the shop door, asked whether we were still waiting. We'd go in; she'd message when the bus came. I picked up my bag and hurried after him."),
        1: ('我们约的地方换过一次，上回在桥那边，这次是电影院旁边的红门小店。我刚才只发了红门，她问哪一个，我才想起附近还有另一家。陈宇把店里的菜单递给我，我照着上面的店名补发过去，又拍了一张门口照片。她说自己还记着上次过桥的路，我赶紧回不用过桥，沿着小路到电影院旁边。消息发完，服务员问我们几个人，我伸出三根手指，说还有一个在路上，先给我们找个里面的位置。', "We'd changed venues: last time beyond the bridge, this time the red-door shop beside the cinema. I'd only texted 'red door.' When she asked which one, I remembered the other nearby shop. Chen Yu handed me the menu so I could send the name and a doorway photo. She still remembered crossing the bridge; I replied that she should follow the path beside the cinema without crossing it. A server asked how many of us there were. Three, I said, with one still on the way; could we sit further inside?"),
        4: ('聊演出时，她说另一场结尾不是不好，是她没听懂。我只听到不好，刚要说那就别推荐了，又停下来问后面是什么。她把话说完，问主角为什么把信留在桌上。我拿出节目单，指着人物名字问是不是姐姐，她摇头，说是后来回家的妹妹。陈宇在旁边问哪场戏，我们两个一起翻那张纸，才发现谁也没记下写信的人。她说下次见小周问问，他那天从头看到尾，也许还记得。', "Discussing another show, she said the ending wasn't bad; she hadn't understood it. I caught 'bad' and nearly said not to recommend it, then asked for the rest. She wanted to know why the lead left the letter on the table. Was it the elder sister? No, the younger one who came home later. Chen Yu asked which scene. Checking the programme together, we realised neither of us had noted who wrote the letter. We'd ask Xiao Zhou, who'd watched the whole show and might remember."),
        5: ('原来她说的妹妹和我记得的姐姐，都穿过同一件外套。我还指着窗边那一场，她已经说到妹妹回家以后了。陈宇笑着问这件衣服到底借过几次，我说先别管衣服，把回家那场再讲一遍。林安从进门说起，讲到把信放下，我终于接上自己看过的那一段。她问这回知道是谁了吧，我说知道，妹妹。她把节目单推回来，让我在名字旁边画个圈，省得下一次又从外套猜起。', "The younger sister she meant and the elder one I remembered had worn the same coat. I was still thinking of the window scene; she'd moved on to the younger sister coming home. How often had that coat been borrowed? Chen Yu laughed. Forget the coat for now—tell the homecoming scene again. From the entrance to putting down the letter, I finally connected it to what I'd seen. The younger sister, then? Yes. She pushed the programme back and had me circle the name so I wouldn't start with the coat again next time."),
        6: ('回家路上，我把她的几条语音又听了一遍。店里的笑声录得特别清楚，先别点后面那句水可以先拿反而不大听得见。我把耳机戴好，再听一次才接上。她最后发文字，说下次店名写全，别只发门的颜色。我回好，又想起刚才妹妹和姐姐的外套，把节目单从包里拿出来看了一眼。陈宇发来明天吃饭的时间，我读完才发现又换了店，赶紧问他店名和地址，先别只告诉我门长什么样。', "On the way home I replayed her messages. The laughter had recorded clearly, but 'water is fine' after 'don't order yet' was hard to hear. With my earphones properly in, I caught it on another listen. Her final text asked for the full shop name next time, rather than the door's colour. I agreed, then checked the programme again, remembering the sisters' coat. Chen Yu sent tomorrow's meal time, at yet another shop. I asked for its name and address before he could tell me only what the door looked like."),
    })
    edits[11]['-paired-reading'].update({
        0: ('我今天的演出比陈宇他们那场晚结束一点，跑到车站，等的车还没来。群里问还要等我吗，我先发你们进去，别站门口。电话接通，朋友却问是不是不来了。我说不是不去，车还没到，晚点来。他那边正有人笑，没听清，我又提高声音重复了一遍。看着站牌，我也着急，可车还没来，只好先把晚点到三个字打出来，再让他们给我留一把椅子，不用一起站在外面吹风。', "My show ended a little later than Chen Yu's group, and the bus still hadn't come when I ran to the stop. Asked whether they should wait, I texted them to go inside. On the phone, a friend thought I wasn't coming. I was, just later—the bus wasn't there yet. Laughter at his end drowned me out, so I repeated it louder. I was anxious too, but could only text that I'd arrive late and ask them to save a chair rather than stand outside in the wind."),
        2: ('朋友问要不要替我点吃的，我说先别点，路上也许会买一点。他又问到了以后再看吗，我说对，水可以先拿。刚说完，车到了，我把手机放进口袋，上去找座位。旁边有人拿着面包，我才发现自己也饿了，可两只手还要拿包和扶住椅背，只好先坐下来。朋友发来菜单照片，我看了两眼，回他说到了自己选，别急着点，我还没看完。他回了个好，旁边又发来一只装水的杯子。', "Asked whether they should order for me, I said not yet; I might buy something on the way. I'd choose when I arrived, but water was fine. The bus came as I finished, and I put my phone away to board. Someone had bread, reminding me how hungry I was, but I needed both hands for my bag and the seat back. Once seated I looked at the menu photo my friend sent. I'd choose there—don't order before I'd finished reading. He agreed and sent a picture of a glass of water."),
        3: ('下车后我沿着小路走，差点又往桥上去。上次的路太熟，我走了几步才想起这次不用过桥，就停下来打开照片。电影院旁边的小店正好有人出来，红门和照片里一样。我给朋友发到了，避开门口等座位的人往里面走。大家已经坐好，旁边空着一把椅子，桌上还有我的水。朋友问是不是又走错门，我说差一点，你下次直接把店名写出来吧。他把菜单递给我，说先吃，吃完我慢慢念给你听。', "After getting off, I nearly followed the familiar route over the bridge. Remembering I didn't need to cross it, I stopped to check the photo. Someone was leaving the cinema-side shop; its red door matched. I texted that I'd arrived and went around the people waiting outside. My chair and water were ready. Had I gone to the wrong door again? Almost—write the shop name next time. He handed me the menu: eat first, then he'd read it very slowly to me."),
        4: ('喝过水我们才谈演出。我说结尾不是不好，是我没听懂，朋友马上问哪句没听清。我笑着说这次听清了，只是不明白妹妹为什么把信留下。他说不是姐姐吗，我拿出节目单，指着妹妹的名字，让他想想后来回家那场。他看了半天，说自己好像漏了那一小段。我把记得的几句讲给他听，又问他前面的写信那场怎么样。这回轮到我想不起来，我们只好把节目单摊在桌上，从人物名字重新对一遍。', "Over water I said the ending wasn't bad; I hadn't understood it. Which line hadn't I heard? My friend asked. This time I'd heard it; I didn't understand why the younger sister left the letter. Wasn't it the elder one? I pointed to the younger sister on the programme and the homecoming scene. He thought he'd missed that short section. I recounted what I remembered and asked about the earlier letter-writing scene. That was the part I couldn't recall, so we spread the programme on the table and checked the names together."),
        5: ('聊到后来，刚才和我对节目单的朋友说，他以前看过前半场，后半场没看完；我却漏了开头，刚才问谁写信，正好问到自己没看的地方。陈宇在旁边拿手机找演出的日期，我看了一眼时间，说今天先别回去了，明天还要早起。他说不是现在，只想下次有空三个人一起看完整。我说好，日期以后再定，这回从开头坐到结束。服务员过来问还要什么，我们看着桌上剩下的菜，赶紧说不用了，先把这些吃完，吃完就各自回家。', "The friend I'd checked the programme with had previously seen the first half but not all of the second; I'd missed the opening, including the letter-writing I'd asked about. Beside us, Chen Yu checked performance dates on his phone. We shouldn't go back tonight—we needed an early start. Not tonight, he said; sometime the three of us could watch the whole thing together. We left the date open and agreed to stay from start to finish. Asked if we wanted anything else, we looked at the food still on the table: finish this, then go home."),
    })
    edits[12]['-r'].update({
        0: ('短剧最后一幕在车站，主角把一封信递给要走的朋友。她接过来，放进包，没有拆。灯慢慢暗下来，旁边的歌唱到门还没关。我坐在第三排，看见她拉好包带，回头望了一眼，觉得信里肯定是在叫她别走。散场后我把这个想法讲给陈宇，他问哪一句写了别走。我翻节目单找了半天，没有找到。他笑着说刚才连信都没拆，你怎么看到里面的字。我只好把节目单合上，说好吧，那是我猜的。', "In the final station scene, the lead handed a letter to the departing friend. She put it in her bag without opening it. As the lights dimmed, the song mentioned an open door. From the third row, her tightened strap and backward glance made me sure the letter asked her not to leave. Afterwards Chen Yu asked which line said that. I searched the programme without finding it. She hadn't even opened the letter—how had I seen its words? I closed the programme and admitted it was my guess."),
        1: ('陈宇问我为什么这样猜，我说她回头时停了好一会儿，歌也还没结束。他倒觉得那封信是让她到了以后再看，因为前面她说过到了再告诉你。我拿节目单指给他看，问那桌边写信写了那么久呢，他说所以才有很多话，不一定只写别走。我们从最后一幕又讲回前面，越讲越想再看一次。旁边一个朋友插进来，说你们两个猜了半天，还没问演戏的人。我们一起转头，才发现林安已经拿着水出来了。', "Why had I guessed that? Her backward glance lasted, and the song wasn't over. Chen Yu thought she might read the letter after arriving, recalling 'I'll tell you when I get there.' What about the long letter-writing scene? There could be plenty to say beyond asking her to stay. We talked backwards through the play and increasingly wanted another viewing. A friend interrupted: we'd spent all this time guessing without asking the actors. Turning around, we found Lin An had already emerged with water."),
        3: ('我还想再听一遍歌，问能不能从灯还亮着那句再来。林安看了看表，说九点半了，十点关门，先收东西吧。陈宇把设备关掉，我和朋友把椅子搬回墙边，刚才坐过的地方一下空了。到了门口，林安轻声唱起今晚这句已经有人听见，我跟着接后面，却又忘了词。她把节目单递给我，上面写着把下一页留给下一次见面。我照着唱完，问下一次是哪天，她说现在还不知道，先让我明天坐上车吧。', "Could we sing again from 'the light is still on'? Lin An checked the time: 9:30, with closing at ten; we'd pack first. Chen Yu shut down the equipment while we carried chairs to the wall. At the door she quietly sang 'someone has heard this line tonight.' I tried to join but forgot the words again. Her programme supplied 'leave the next page for our next meeting.' After singing it, I asked when that would be. She didn't know yet—first let her catch tomorrow's train."),
        4: ('第二天我八点半到车站入口，带了一瓶水。林安拉着箱子过来，问其他人呢，我说几个要上班，今天就我来。她接过水，让我帮她拿一下包，自己把箱子上的节目单收进去。我们站到不挡人的地方，又聊昨晚那封信，她还是让我自己猜。我问到了以后能不能告诉我们一声，她说可以，到了就在群里发消息。九点的车快开了，她拿回包，挥挥手走进入口。我站了一会儿，才发现自己手里还拿着没打开的另一瓶水。', "At 8:30 I met Lin An at the station entrance with water. Where were the others? Some had work; it was just me. She had me hold her bag while she packed the programme from her suitcase. Standing out of the way, we discussed the letter again; she still left me to guess. Could she let us know when she arrived? Yes, she'd message the group. With the nine o'clock train nearing departure, she took back her bag and waved. After watching her go, I noticed the other unopened bottle still in my hand."),
    })
